commit ed16761804e7d015e359d9997a2835e11517db65

C03: known folders can be listed on request, names only (FILES1425 infrastructure, BUILD1425)

The owner's folder listings (H0201/H0264 «lista los archivos del escritorio», H0329/H0698 «qué hay en Descargas») had no operation: filesystem.list is confined to the sandbox and filesystem.known.search needs a name to look for. The owner authorized the known-folder provider on 2026-09-13.

Baxy.Kernel ProductCatalog: filesystem.known.list (folder ∈ desktop/documents/downloads, limit 1..100), read-only, public, "windows.toplevel.identities.v1".
Baxy.Core ExternalCapabilityHandlers: the operation is routed to the external provider.
Baxy.Providers.Windows WindowsKnownFileAdapter.List: top-level entries of the named known folder (name, kind, size, modifiedUtc; folders first, then names), hidden and system entries skipped, no paths, count/fileCount/folderCount, bounded by the limit, authority windows_known_folder_toplevel_postread; WindowsExternalCapabilityProvider names the required adapter.
Baxy.App ObservedResponseLiterals: listed names are observed data (dots, hyphens and underscores included); MindSidecarClient: a listing is a dense output (ten-second budget).
baxy_mind effect_intent: _known_folder_listing_request reads the whole-folder listing forms (list/show/tell the files of…, what is in…) and owns the folder enum; __main__ grounds folder and limit 100 without literal words; llm projects the receipt to folder label, counts and six names, instructs one quotation per name, and vetoes listing_unlisted_name/listing_wrong_count; observed_response_literals masks the listed names.

Offline probe: the four literals and five variants resolve to filesystem.known.list with the right folder; definitions, a prohibition, a name search and the screen question do not; a faithful listing passes the vetoes, an invented name or count does not. Product compiled (BUILD1425). Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


